# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deny list — keep internal repo files off the public site.
#
# This Cloudflare Pages project is git-connected and serves the repo root
# directly, so every tracked file (docs, scripts, tests, fixtures) used to be
# publicly fetchable. Pages _redirects rules are always followed even when a
# physical file matches, so each rule below masks an internal path by
# redirecting it to the app home. Rewrites to a hard 404 are not supported by
# Pages; a 302 to "/" stops raw content delivery, which is the goal here.
#
# Everything NOT listed below stays public on purpose — index.html and the
# data exports the dashboard fetches (data/shared/* and the root JSON copies
# that loaders fall back to). If you add a root-level script or doc, it is
# automatically denied by the extension wildcards at the bottom of this file.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Root config / dotfiles (never served)
